# What never reaches a build context (WP-22).
#
# The context is the repository root for every image in docker/, so this file decides how much is
# sent to the daemon and — more importantly — what *cannot* end up in a layer by accident. Two of
# the entries are security rather than speed: `.env` holds real values on a developer's machine
# (BD-002), and `.git` carries every value the repository ever had, including one deleted in a
# later commit.
#
# `node_modules` is excluded and re-created inside the image: a host install is the wrong platform
# (`@node-rs/argon2` and the Agent SDK ship per-OS, per-arch binaries) and would silently produce
# an image that cannot start.
#
# Anchored to the context root with a leading `/` where a root match is meant, for the same reason
# `.gitignore` is (CLAUDE.md): an unanchored pattern matches at any depth, and `dist` unanchored
# would drop `apps/web/dist`, which one stage builds and the next copies.

.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Secrets and local state, never in a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Generated output that a stage rebuilds anyway; excluded so a stale host build cannot be copied.
/apps/web/dist
/apps/runlet/dist
/coverage
/playwright-report
/test-results
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Developer and agent scratch space.
/.claude
/.vscode
/.idea
.DS_Store
